                        "target_lang_word": "neverending",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "neverending",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9eda205a-9f99-3d6d-a799-6240907c548f",
                                        "entry_id": "c1438b17-50d6-36f3-8f6a-951288ffa7f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having no end or being endless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a204f896-9c9b-4626-bcdb-8514e5458cd9",
                                                "sense_id": "9eda205a-9f99-3d6d-a799-6240907c548f",
                                                "text": "Lulling music washed around me, soft voices announced the rising and falling of airliners, huge screens clicked soothingly through neverending arrivals and departures."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "779de9ff-c497-4618-879f-8075bb736e46",
                        "source_entry_id": "553b6553-694d-32fa-85db-4857891f5d72",
                        "source_sense_id": "9d511e89-b284-369f-ae52-c5d7a0757657",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Sens figuré) Incessant.",
                        "target_lang_word": "never-ending",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "never-ending",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cd6b8dfa-959b-30d5-b704-fd0d4548f369",
                                        "entry_id": "43aa539f-1afa-3c03-9b09-90f3c38609df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of neverending."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0abc3b3-3131-4ce4-a556-5fe703d7f91a",
                                                "sense_id": "cd6b8dfa-959b-30d5-b704-fd0d4548f369",
                                                "text": "The story of upkeep has been never-ending. Between 1997-2000, a major programme of maintenance entailed replacing superstructure timbers - 50 main rail beams were replaced with greenheart, along with a similar number of edge beams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83a4a23c-bcc8-47cb-95bd-aaa5e704b2e7",
                                                "sense_id": "cd6b8dfa-959b-30d5-b704-fd0d4548f369",
                                                "text": "But fans’ emotions are no longer filtered through ticket or album sales; they’re heard directly, constantly, at all hours, on all the platforms people visit to generate and extinguish bad feelings in a never-ending cycle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c4929621-0c30-4aef-b500-aabb1b25a7ac",
                        "source_entry_id": "553b6553-694d-32fa-85db-4857891f5d72",
                        "source_sense_id": "9d511e89-b284-369f-ae52-c5d7a0757657",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Sens figuré) Incessant.",
                        "target_lang_word": "incessant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incessant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2eb82fa7-5f8f-3812-95c7-1d743e66e5c6",
                                        "entry_id": "8c051f11-22d9-3ac7-964e-df30df03d9e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without pause or stop; not ending, especially to the point of annoyance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f309daf4-df23-4a23-86dd-3d0bc76205d0",
                                                "sense_id": "2eb82fa7-5f8f-3812-95c7-1d743e66e5c6",
                                                "text": "The dog's incessant barking kept the girl awake all night."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d99ba1c0-f99b-40ad-8ab2-5780973fa96c",
                                                "sense_id": "2eb82fa7-5f8f-3812-95c7-1d743e66e5c6",
                                                "text": "[…] incessant interferings and bickerings, in every country, between the secular powers and the ecclesiastical."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53079081-c0da-4cd5-a07f-532113bfc88c",
                                                "sense_id": "2eb82fa7-5f8f-3812-95c7-1d743e66e5c6",
                                                "text": "The face of Nature may be compared to a yielding surface, with ten thousand sharp wedges packed close together and driven inwards by incessant blows, sometimes one wedge being struck, and then another with greater force."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
